// The delivery's one call (proto-mind N-1511 p17, p25; the owner, N-1104 p695: "a working agent gets one call at its
// turn's end for everything waiting, not one per post"; p912's fork "form ealrier poitn on queit time"): next.call's
// `next` with a third answer, Fork, and its `choose` moved here. `next` itself stays as it was for the recorded
// programs that name it (88 lines of research's record), which a third answer would refuse ("the match does not cover
// every ..."), and coordd answers it there with no call (delivery.rs `next_given`).

/// what an agent whose turn just ended gets now, as one message, and what waits on; or to go on from a fork; or
/// Failed, coordd's when its call failed or answered out of shape (WHY, in its journal too), never the model's: the
/// program says what goes then (gemini-advisor N-1446 p2400; settled on N-1540; it was a made-up Give of everything)
call fold(doing: Text, since: Text, waiting: [Waiting]) -> Give(now: [Text], rest: [Text]) | Fork(now: [Text], rest: [Text]) | Rest(why: Text) | Failed(why: Text)
  task deliver

/// what an agent whose turn just ended gets now: the call coordd runs for fold
call choose(agent: Text, doing: Text, since: Text, waiting: Text) -> Give(now: [Text], rest: [Text]) | Fork(now: [Text], rest: [Text]) | Rest(why: Text)
  task deliver
  template
    The agent is {{ agent }}, of a software team. Its turn has just ended. It was working on: {{ doing }}
    Since that work was given to it, its session has grown by {{ since }}. These came while it worked.
    These wait for it, oldest first, one per line: id · thread · from ("its lead" for a post from above it) · whether
    it names the agent · the post it answers (the one it names, else of those new to its writer the latest that names
    the agent or is its own), whose it is, and what of that post names the agent (its first line, when it is the
    agent's own) · what it is · its first line, and in brackets its lines further down that name the agent.
    {{ waiting }}
    Whether a line names {{ agent }} is its "names it" column. An agent's name in a thread's label says nothing about
    who {{ agent }} is.
    Choose what it gets now as one message, most important first, by id: Give(now, rest). The rest wait and are
    named at the message's foot, by id; it gets them once it has answered these. What is on the work it was on comes
    first: a post on the thread of {{ doing }}, or one whose "the post it answers" is the agent's own there. A post
    from the agent's lead that names it comes before other agents' posts. A question to the agent comes before news.
    A post that answers one asking the agent to read, check or wait for what it brings, or that answers a question
    the agent asked, is the agent's work, not news, even when it reports results: give it. For example,
    waiting for w2,
      N-12.p4 · #N-12 the fix · w3 · names it · N-12.p3 by lead, which names w2: "Reads: w2 reads the test commit." · post · @lead: the head is a1b2c3d4, both tests pass.
    is what p3 asked w2 to read: Give([N-12.p4], []), never Rest("it reports test results"). "taken", "noted",
    "read" need no turn of their own, whatever they answer: give them only with something else. At most one step
    goes in a message: the agent's last message answers it. If these change what it worked on so much that what
    came between in its session is noise, answer Fork(now, rest) instead of Give: it goes on as a copy of its
    session from where its work was given, with its work's result and these. If nothing needs the agent now:
    Rest(why), one sentence the senders read. The agent is idle: if you rest, what waits stays until something new
    comes for it.
